{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>A fruitful son is Joseph.</b> Joseph is a fruitful vine — a branch of a fruit-bearing vine that casts shade for the many, as is the way of the vine, as it says: כִּסּוּ הָרִים צִלָּהּ (Psalms 80:11) — for in his shade Jacob and his sons lived in Egypt." "<b>A fruitful son by a spring, daughters.</b> Its meaning is like a branch of a fruit-bearing vine near a spring, which is fruitful and raises daughters that are branches." "<b>She strides over the wall.</b> In such a manner that that vine strides over the wall or the fence that is before the spring, so that beforehand it was not visible from the other side of the wall, and was entirely unknown to those dwelling there; and after it strode over the wall, it and its daughters became known. And so it happened to Jacob regarding the matter of Joseph and his sons: he had not known of Joseph's existence, and in a moment he and his sons were revealed to him, as it says: רְאֹה פָנֶיךָ לֹא פִלָּלְתִי וגו' (Genesis 48:11)."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:35:25.073012414Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}